From 590c9ef297cef1ca7d0292d56b16536b8bcf184d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rkvenc forward-port <forward-port@local>
Date: Sat, 4 Jul 2026 23:14:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 15/39] media: rockchip: harden IOMMU forward port

Restore the BSP large-segment DMA contract in the Rockchip/VSI IOMMU providers, preserve provider fault fallback semantics, and guard provider MMIO helpers with runtime-PM state.

Make RGA and MPP reject unsafe DMA mappings before programming hardware: mappings must be a single nonzero, non-wrapping 32-bit IOVA span.

Clean up MPP shared-domain, fixed-window, clock/runtime-PM, run-failure, AV1 AFBC IRQ, RKVENC DCHS, and slice-wait unwind paths found during adversarial review.
